{"availability":"available","full":"HieuTong/budgetbasket-ai","name":"budgetbasket-ai","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Finance","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-02T06:14:32Z","updated":"2026-10-11T02:09:03Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://budgetbasket-ai.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://budgetbasket-ai.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:06.404Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:06.404Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:06.404Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T02:10:06.404Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A cost-of-living optimizer for Australian households: given your usual purchases and a budget, it builds a shopping basket that stays close to your habits while cutting cost — using classical ML, retrieval-augmented generation, and an agentic tool-calling layer, not just a single LLM prompt.","Grocery prices in Australia have risen sharply, and most \"AI shopping\" demos are thin wrappers around a chat prompt. This project is built to show the opposite: a real optimization algorithm at the core, with ML and LLM components layered around it where they're actually the right tool — not used everywhere for effect.","Google's Gemini API has a genuine free tier (1,500 requests/day on Flash, no billing method required) as of 2026 — OpenAI's API doesn't reliably offer one anymore (small trial credits, if issued at all, expire in 3 months and typically still require adding a card). Function calling is done manually here (JSON-schema tool declarations, parsed functioncall parts) rather than via the SDK's automatic function-calling feature, to keep the agent's control flow explicit — see the docstring in app/agent/agent.py."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HieuTong/budgetbasket-ai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1d4aba0ab4d4d4f961859fd04e781fc1af39eee369e9a05f9bb53ffc445bd